    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_0e662a6fc863f550cd90b801624bbadbc33eb7eee42ee102806a54d6f773660e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Primitive dual vectors encode principal horizons; Mobius inversion removes primitivity and inserts a reciprocal Riemann-zeta factor into the Mellin representation. Formally shifting that contour then makes residues at zeta zeros govern the small-scatterer remainder, and the same horizon sum enters diffusivity through the survival-diffusion relation, carrying the formal RH-sensitive remainder to D.",
