    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_30998772582d150f1631061eb65a8c26a02ee17faeacf06d145da46a5e981057",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source has a layered evidence chain: geometric lemmas prove finiteness of maximal horizons and the contribution of one non-incipient horizon; global survival and diffusion theorems are conditional on separate maximal-dominance and decorrelation conjectures; simulations test selected finite-dimensional consequences; the critical-dimension law adds a heuristic summability extrapolation; and the RH-sensitive small-scatterer remainder adds an unproved Mellin-contour step.",
