    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c46b1d9f4ee1c1f9fb2f8bddb3cc106c766d94913c6a8fc008e41ea659a9347c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For a non-incipient horizon of dimension d_H, the proved single-horizon calculation gives survival of order t^{-(d-d_H)}; Conjecture 1 promotes the finite sum over maximal horizons to the global survival law, and Conjecture 3 promotes collision-free constant-velocity contributions to the leading correlation. Consequently only principal horizons, with codimension one, yield the 1/t correlation scale that integrates to logarithmic superdiffusion.",
