    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_cd0f431cccdc6bc01a83b7dadb586a2ce89b81ec86524119cea802605b482dd9",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "At the touching transition, an incipient principal horizon has zero direct measure but contains countably many codimension-two subordinate horizons. Rescaling their cross-sections yields an individual contribution proportional to 1/(t^2 L^5); summing over lattice directions converges through dimension five and diverges from dimension six, providing a geometric summability mechanism for a critical change in survival decay.",
