    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ce5c45730a612a8e92279ddc12daa62c12b86002d3e38f279d2a45c8dc3dcfbb",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "In logarithmic superdiffusion, the Gaussian core controls weak convergence while expanding ballistic tails remain visible at finite time and supply the part of the second moment not represented by that core; the source's tail-balance argument therefore predicts that the limiting Gaussian covariance Xi equals D rather than the normal-diffusion relation Xi=2D.",
